    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. I'm looking closer at Jax and Andre specifically. You mentioned they fit the gritty crime vibe, but I'm worried I'm being too predictable with them. \n\nIn a typical crime drama, what is the 'expected' role or personality for someone like Jax (street smart, hood up) vs someone like Andre (knows everyone on the corner)? Like, if I wanted to keep the show grounded in realism, is it more 'accurate' to have them as the muscle/street-level informants, or could they be something else? I'm just trying to see if their backgrounds naturally pull them toward certain types of roles in that genre.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
