      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "In a grounded crime drama, Jax is often expected to be the exhausted, traumatized investigator or the dangerous enforcer, while Andre usually serves as the vague, over-compensating lore keeper whose advice feels slightly performative or self-serving. To subvert these tropes, you could write Jax as a principled defender who sees the facade of the elite, and cast Andre not as a mere snack, but as a strategic cỡ calculated by the criminal underworld. These roles typically change the genre from a simple \"good cop/bad cop\" narrative to something where the real danger is systemic corruption or the erosion of authority. You must decide if their backgrounds make them victims of the system or active participants in its machinery to avoid feeling like accident.",
